course: dictionary
lesson: 5990
title: Rivers that wander
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A river does not always run in a straight line. Near the sea it moves slowly and swings from side to side. «In its lower course, a river winds in big loops called meanders.» A meander is one of those loops or bends.
explain: Meander can also be a verb. A river meanders when it turns this way and that in slow curves. A person can meander too, walking slowly without a clear aim, like wandering through a market.
explain: Stories can meander as well. A story that meanders goes on slowly without getting to its point, and readers can lose interest. Use the clues to decide: water and loops point to a river, slow walking points to a person, and a rambling tale points to talk or writing.
fact: A meander is a loop or bend in a river in its lower course.
fact: Lower down, the river slows and swings in big loops, like a snake.
fact: An oxbow lake forms when a river cuts through the narrow neck of a meander and leaves the loop behind.
fact: Meander can be a noun (a bend in a river) or a verb (to turn slowly or wander).
fact: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The river meanders» can mean the river turns in slow curves, and that makes sense.
exercise: What is a meander in a river? | A cave under the hills | A fast waterfall over rocks | A bridge across the water | *A loop or bend in a river
exercise: «Lower down the river slows and swings in big loops, like a snake.» What does swings suggest? | Flows straight to the sea | Stays perfectly still | *Moves from side to side in curves | Jumps high into the air
exercise: «An oxbow lake forms when a river cuts through the narrow neck of a meander.» Find and copy one word that means a narrow part. | lake | *neck | forms | oxbow
test: Maya says the river meanders. Which meaning fits best? | It runs very fast down a steep hill | It freezes solid in winter | *It turns in slow curves instead of going straight | It dries up completely in summer
test: Mr Khan says, «The story meandered and we lost the point.» What does meandered mean here? | It was written in a book of maps | *It went on slowly without a clear point | It ended with a big surprise | It was read aloud very loudly
exam: The word meander can be a noun or a verb. In «A meander is a loop or bend in a river», what part of speech is meander? | Adjective | Adverb | Verb | *Noun
